{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgmmz2t5nr4X5FhWACqBT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Which I'd rather see: Option A (\"א. עמודה לכל דרך\").** I noticed the designers marked it \"מומלץ\", but that's not why I picked it. It has one short line that tells me what this costs me: \"300 ₪ בחודש מכם, 900 ₪ מהמעסיק\". Option B leaves that line out.\n\n## 1. What I'd do, and how sure I am\n\nI'd join. My reasoning, in my own words: 300 shekels a month comes off my pay, and my employer adds 900 that I wouldn't get otherwise. After 5 years that's \"66,513 ₪\" in the fund against \"19,595 ₪\" if I'd invested the same 300 myself. The sentence that settled it was \"כל שקל שהפקדתם נהיה ₪ 3.70 בקרן ו-₪ 1.09 בחשבון ניירות ערך\". I understood that sentence on the first read.\n\nI'm about 80% sure. The rest is doubt about my age. The page says that before 6 years \"מס\", and from 6 years \"פטור ממס\". At 61, six years takes me to 67. If I need the money sooner, the page shows tax of \"−13,974 ₪\" at year 5, more than all the profit. I'd still come out far ahead, but I'd like to know my real situation.\n\n## 2. Parts I actually used\n\n- The title and the line under it, \"רצועת השנים נשארת, עכשיו בצבעים…\".\n- In Option A: the 5-year picture, the toggle set to \"שכירים\", the \"כל שקל…\" sentence, and the two big totals marked \"נשאר בידיים\".\n- The second copy, \"אותו ציור שנה אחת אחר כך\", for year 6. The tax there is \"0 ₪\" and the total is \"98,738 ₪\". That jump of about 32,000 shekels in one year told me to wait the full 6 years.\n- The orange warning in the fine print: \"⚠ הנחה: אתם 2.5% והמעסיק 7.5%… האחוזים האמיתיים כתובים בהסכם העבודה\". It was useful, because it tells me to check my own contract.\n\n## 3. Block by block\n\n1. **Title and subtitle.** Read them. \"בלי כדורים ובלי טבלה\" means nothing to me, because I never saw the old version.\n2. **\"מה היה\" small picture.** Skipped it. It's tiny and I can't read it. Why show me something that isn't there anymore?\n3. **Fine print under it (\"הדוגמה: שכר ברוטו 12,000 ₪…\").** I read every word and understood about half. The salary, the percentages and \"7% בשנה\" were fine. The rest confused me: \"מיטב השתלמות עוקב מדד S&P500 (13245)\", \"ילין לפידות מחקה\", \"(5139282)\", \"(4D)\", \"פייר פיננשיאל טכנולוג'יז\".\n4. **Option A, 5 years.** Used it, and it was my main block.\n5. **Option A, year 6 copy.** Used it. It was the most convincing part.\n6. **Option B, \"ב. כל חלק בעמודה משלו\".** Read it and compared. The tax looks clearer here, because it's drawn as a step down. But the parts run left to right, so I met \"נשאר בידיים\" before the start. I also lost the \"300 ₪ בחודש מכם\" line, and the left chart has no ₪ signs.\n7. **Last screenshot.** Empty, nothing there.\n\n## 4. In the charts\n\n- **Looked at:** the grey \"ההפקדות שלכם\", the yellow \"הפקדות המעסיק\", the green \"רווח אחרי דמי ניהול\", and the pink striped \"מס במשיכה\" with its minus sign. I also looked at the big totals and the labels \"לפני 6 שנים: מס\" and \"מ-6 שנים: פטור ממס\".\n- **12-year strip:** I mostly used it to see that the bars get much taller after year 6. I didn't study each year.\n- **Ignored:** the \"עצמאים\" button (I'm salaried), the dotted lines under the numbers, and the white bracket beside the bars.\n- **Confused me:** in Option A the striped tax block sits *on top of* the column. My first thought was that it's money added. Only the minus sign told me otherwise. It's also two colours, orange-striped and green-striped, and I don't know why.\n\n## 5. What I didn't understand\n\n- Why the tax at year 5 (13,974) is bigger than the whole profit (8,487). Is my employer's money taxed too?\n- \"דמי ניהול\", \"מסלולים\", \"תעריפים\", \"מחקה\", \"עד התקרה בחוק\", \"הכול בכסף של היום\".\n- The ID numbers in brackets in the fine print.\n- The line \"בין 14 התעריפים שנאספו: 10,764 ₪ … עד 19,595 ₪\". So the 19,595 shown is the best case? Then the account could be half that.\n\n## 6. What I wanted and couldn't find\n\n- **My age:** can I take the money without tax when I retire, even before 6 years? At 61 this matters most to me.\n- **Leaving my job:** what happens if I change jobs or stop working before 6 years?\n- **Not joining:** do I get the 900 in my salary instead, or is it simply lost?\n- **My paycheck:** how much less will actually reach my bank each month?\n- **Bad years:** what if the market falls? The page assumes 7% every year.\n- **My own numbers:** a place to put in my real salary instead of 12,000.\n\n## 7. If half the page had to go\n\n1. The \"מה היה\" small picture.\n2. Option B, since I picked A. I'd keep B's way of showing tax as a step down, though.\n3. The fund and fee names and numbers in the fine print. I'd keep only the assumptions and the orange warning.\n4. The \"עצמאים\" toggle, for someone like me.\n\nI'd keep the year-6 copy. That's the part that told me what to do with my money."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7435,"cache_read_input_tokens":3684,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7435},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03e1f1a5-c88b-411e-aaa2-ee112b6bfd9b","uuid":"4d4968b6-b6d0-480f-889a-22492f56c52c","timestamp":"2026-11-06T13:46:41.496Z","request_id":"req_011Cgmmz2bioMjwDhqUdfZ4a"}
